                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 661.939/18</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-02T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1918,
                                noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.55
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Legation’s telegram June 24, 4 p.m. Under instructions of his Government French
                    Minister is urging upon the Chinese Government resumption of embargo on exports
                    to Siberia and informs me that the Chinese Government is prepared to accede if
                    such action is deemed necessary as a war measure by the Allies. The British and
                    Japanese legations are disposed to support French representations. French
                    Minister expresses the hope in view of new situation created by the action of
                    the Czecho-Slovak troops at Vladivostok and west of Irkutsk our Government may
                    consider it advisable to modify the policy indicated in your telegram of June
                    10, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>I beg to request early instructions as to your views as British Minister, as dean
                    of the Allied representatives, is endeavoring to delay further action by his
                    colleagues until I am in position to state whether or not recent developments
                    have induced any alteration in your attitude towards this question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >MacMurray</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
